# mpd.env — per-project configuration for an astro project.
# Seeded from this project type's template/ at `mpd create <project>` time and
# never overwritten afterwards. Edit directly, or via
# `mpd configure <project> KEY=VALUE` (mpd sanitises and rewrites lines).
#
# Keys are namespaced MPD_<RUNTIME>_<TYPE>_<KEY>. Per-project values here
# override anything set in /var/lib/mpd/env/mpd-vm.env. This file — like
# everything else in the type's template/ — is auto-added to
# .git/info/exclude.

# Database engine + version. Astro is a static-site generator and uses no
# database — explicit empty value here blocks fall-through to any
# MPD_DB=... that the developer may have set in mpd-vm.env.
MPD_DB=""

# There is no port setting here on purpose. mpd reads the dev-server port
# from `server.port` in astro.config.mjs (falling back to Astro's 4321) and
# points caddy at it. Since mpd does not start the server, a second setting
# here could only move caddy's upstream while the server kept binding what
# its own config says — so set the port in astro.config.mjs and re-run
# `mpd configure <project>`.
#
# Two astro projects in one runtime need different ports: whichever starts
# second cannot bind an address the first already holds.
